From: Oever Gonzalez <software@notengobattery.com>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: airoha: expose the thermal zone through hwmon

DT-registered thermal zones no longer get a hwmon device implicitly;
each driver must opt in. Mirror mediatek auxadc/lvts so lm-sensors can
read the SoC temperature.

--- a/drivers/thermal/airoha_thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/airoha_thermal.c
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/thermal.h>
 
+#include "thermal_hwmon.h"
+
 /* SCU regs */
 #define EN7581_PLLRG_PROTECT			0x268
 #define EN7581_PWD_TADC				0x2ec
@@ -689,6 +691,8 @@ static int airoha_thermal_probe(struct p
 		return PTR_ERR(priv->tz);
 	}
 
+	devm_thermal_add_hwmon_sysfs(dev, priv->tz);
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, priv);
 
 	return soc_data->post_probe ? soc_data->post_probe(pdev) : 0;
